   "excerpt": "Item 8.01 Other Events. In connection with recent lawsuits filed by various shareholders in the Court of Chancery in Delaware, which have been consolidated under the action captioned In Re Meta Platforms, Inc. Class C Reclassification Litigation, Consol. C.A. No. 2026-1413-KSJM (the \u201cShareholder Litigation\u201d), asserting claims challenging the recapitalization of Meta Platforms, Inc. (the \u201cCompany\u201d) with a trial scheduled to begin April 19, 2027, the Company has agreed that it will not issue any shares of Class C common stock, whether through a dividend or otherwise, during the pendency of the pre-trial and trial proceedings in the Court of Chancery. In furtherance of this, Mark Zuckerberg, the Company\u2019s founder, Chairman, and Chief Executive Officer, granted a waiver to the Company of the requirement in the Founder Alignment Agreement, dated October 20, 2026, between the Company and Mr. Z"
